fact WorkItem(id: "WI-601", description: some(value: "Typer ALTITUDE (follow-up to WI-598): unify the abstract-spec-carrier deferral across BOTH dispatch shapes. WI-598 taught the CARRIER-PARAM escape (check_apply_iter ~6271) to defer when the receiver's carrier sort is itself an abstract spec (carrier_is_abstract_spec = no own constructors AND something provides it). But the SELF-RECEIVER path's receiver_carrier (~typing.rs:10454) still classifies Abstract by the NARROWER base==spec_sort test, so a value whose static type is an abstract-spec sort DIFFERENT from the op's spec is returned Concrete(...). Latent gap: a body-less Stream self-receiver op NOT overridden by FiniteStream (e.g. consuming a FiniteStream-typed value through a bare Stream op) concrete-dispatches into FiniteStream provides Stream -> Stream requires EffectsRuntime[E], unsatisfiable at the abstract access row -> the SAME spurious DispatchNoMatch WI-598 fixes. Pre-existing (untested today; finite consumption routes through the carrier-param FiniteCollection.collect). RIGHT DEPTH: have receiver_carrier (or a shared helper both paths call) return Abstract when carrier_is_abstract_spec(base) — funnel both shapes through one notion. Regression-screen: concrete carriers (List/Map, which have constructors) stay Concrete; only abstract-interface carriers newly defer (an improvement, the values are concrete providers at runtime). Needs a self-receiver-on-abstract-spec test + full suite. ACCEPTANCE: a body-less Stream self-receiver op on a FiniteStream-typed value typechecks+evals (defers to eval value-directed dispatch); cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-598"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-01T15:44:25Z"))

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-601", name: "finiteness")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-601", author: "claude", content: "DELIVERED (committed b51ea29, code before review = clobber-safe). receiver_carrier now classifies Abstract when carrier_is_abstract_spec(base) (base != op spec, no own constructors, provided) -> the abstract self-receiver defer arm handles it, exactly the WI-598 carrier-param escape. Full workspace suite green (2393). /code-review (4 agents): SOUND, no bugs. One agent empirically verified by reverting the guard in a worktree (test FAILS pre-fix with the 3 MissingRequiresForSpecOp errors incl Stream.splitFirst.requires, ok post-fix returning 2). Soundness cleared: deferral hands to eval value-directed dispatch on the runtime concrete provider; load-time backing invariant (typing.rs ~9403 concrete-only) + Pass-2 op-table inheritance guarantee the lookup succeeds for direct providers (FiniteMappedStream). Return/effects threaded by projection elimination independent of receiver_carrier, so skipping the Concrete-only bind/effect-close leaks nothing (test's effects fs.E matches structurally). LATENT (NOT this WI, no fix now): (1) self-receiver path still lacks the carrier-param transitive-flag leg -> a concrete carrier providing the op spec only TRANSITIVELY stays Concrete; latent, no stdlib self-receiver op is transitive-only. (2) the abstract defer arm skips the effect-close (pre-existing property of ALL abstract dispatch, not new): a future body-less self-receiver op with a BARE 'effects E' (not s.E projection) on an abstract-spec receiver could surface undeclared ?_; no such stdlib op exists.", at: "2026-07-01T15:44:10Z")
